From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: h264: reject a slice header larger than the slice

header_bit_size comes from userspace and is not checked against the
slice. A large value makes cedrus_skip_bits() flush bits for minutes in
device_run(), with the media device's req_queue_mutex held.

Fail the job when the header is larger than the slice.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
@@ -405,6 +405,9 @@
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_H264_TRIGGER_TYPE,
 		     VE_H264_TRIGGER_TYPE_INIT_SWDEC);
 
+	if (slice->header_bit_size > slice_bytes * 8)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	ret = cedrus_skip_bits(dev, slice->header_bit_size);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
